A FAILING CHECK THAT WAS THE TEST'S FAULT, NOT THE CODE'S
The first run reported "unauthenticated → 401" failing with 500. The route is
not in the proxy.ts allowlist, so an unauthenticated request is redirected 307
to /login before the handler runs; fetch followed that redirect, re-POSTed the
body to /login, and reported that page's status. Confirmed with curl
(status=307 redirect=/login). The assertion was corrected to expect the
redirect, and the fetch now uses redirect: "manual". The route's own getUser()
check remains as defence in depth for if the allowlist ever changes — RLS is
still the actual boundary.

VERIFICATION DEBT
The three Server Actions are NOT exercised. They call cookies() from
next/headers, so they cannot be invoked outside a request context, and there is
no UI yet. Phase 4 builds that UI and is where confirm, remove and the signed
URL get exercised. Until then confirmRentalStatement setting fees_confirmed_at —
the gate that makes fees claimable — is unproven end to end, even though
resolveAgentFees' handling of that column has 19 unit tests.

Only Rich & Oliva statements have been extracted. A different agency's layout
remains unproven, which is what the confirm gate exists for.
